00:25:03,300 --> 00:25:06,300
Wow. They're due to be executed.

548
00:25:06,300 --> 00:25:08,300
Is this the last of the bunch?

549
00:25:08,300 --> 00:25:10,300
Yes, that's so.

550
00:25:10,300 --> 00:25:12,300
Here, let them through.

551
00:25:12,300 --> 00:25:14,300
Thank you, Maytag repairman.

552
00:25:14,300 --> 00:25:15,300
Okay, go ahead.

553
00:25:15,300 --> 00:25:18,300
Where's Unit 3? We're going to live there.

554
00:25:18,300 --> 00:25:21,300
Yes, ma'am. Keep going right over the rise. You'll find Unit 3 on your left.

555
00:25:21,300 --> 00:25:23,300
Thanks.

556
00:25:23,300 --> 00:25:32,300
Russian agents stealthily approach the guard point, see the stop signs and turn around defeated.

557
00:25:32,300 --> 00:25:35,300
Tornado Magnet Trailer Park welcomes you.

558
00:25:35,300 --> 00:25:43,300
Yeah, a lot of loose meat sandwiches eaten here.

559
00:25:43,300 --> 00:25:46,300
Honey, now don't get mad, but I forgot our trailer.

560
00:25:46,300 --> 00:25:49,300
Don't.

561
00:25:49,300 --> 00:25:50,300
Well, this is it, honey.

562
00:25:50,300 --> 00:25:52,300
The end of all hope and joy.

563
00:25:52,300 --> 00:25:54,300
Try to make the best of it.

564
00:25:54,300 --> 00:25:58,300
Come on, kids, let's get out.

565
00:25:58,300 --> 00:26:01,300
Here's the last box of your resentment for me.

566
00:26:01,300 --> 00:26:04,300
Well, I put away most of the clothes. There's good closet space, anyhow.

567
00:26:04,300 --> 00:26:06,300
It's not so bad.

568
00:26:06,300 --> 00:26:09,300
Sure. You like living on the beach.

569
00:26:09,300 --> 00:26:11,300
It's only temporary, Annie.

570
00:26:11,300 --> 00:26:14,300
It doesn't matter. The sand's going to drift in and ruin everything, anyhow.

571
00:26:14,300 --> 00:26:18,300
Look, honey, I've driven over 500 miles today.

572
00:26:18,300 --> 00:26:21,300
Tomorrow I start a new job, an important job.

573
00:26:21,300 --> 00:26:24,300
I'm a little tired myself.

574
00:26:24,300 --> 00:26:26,300
Of course. I'm sorry.

575
00:26:26,300 --> 00:26:28,300
I'm just tight and bitter.

576
00:26:28,300 --> 00:26:30,300
I guess I'm just homesick for San Francisco.

577
00:26:30,300 --> 00:26:34,300
Great life in the Castro district.

578
00:26:34,300 --> 00:26:35,300
Well, where is it?

579
00:26:35,300 --> 00:26:37,300
San Francisco? It's up the coast, I think.

580
00:26:37,300 --> 00:26:39,300
Launching platform.

581
00:26:39,300 --> 00:26:40,300
Sit on the beach?

582
00:26:40,300 --> 00:26:42,300
Probably. Somewhere on the beach.

583
00:26:42,300 --> 00:26:43,300
Everything's on the beach here.

584
00:26:43,300 --> 00:26:44,300
When's the first task?

585
00:26:44,300 --> 00:26:47,300
I don't know. Soon. Maybe this week.

586
00:26:47,300 --> 00:26:48,300
Will it work?

587
00:26:48,300 --> 00:26:50,300
Look, I'm trying to avoid you with menial work, okay?

588
00:26:50,300 --> 00:26:52,300
It's got to.

589
00:26:52,300 --> 00:26:54,300
It's got to do a job better than theirs.

590
00:26:54,300 --> 00:26:55,300
So if they start needing...

591
00:26:55,300 --> 00:26:57,300
Dave, what you said about its accuracy?

592
00:26:57,300 --> 00:27:00,300
We just got here, honey. I don't know any answers.

593
00:27:00,300 --> 00:27:03,300
But you, your company, you worked on it for months.

594
00:27:03,300 --> 00:27:06,300
I worked on one pot out of 35,000 pots.

595
00:27:06,300 --> 00:27:09,300
It's much more complicated than just an intercontinental missile.

596
00:27:09,300 --> 00:27:11,300
It's not like shopping or makeup.

597
00:27:11,300 --> 00:27:13,300
Is ours the only one?

598
00:27:13,300 --> 00:27:15,300
We don't think so.

599
00:27:15,300 --> 00:27:18,300
I enjoy our warm chats about civil defense, honey.

600
00:27:18,300 --> 00:27:20,300
It's almost funny, isn't it?

601
00:27:20,300 --> 00:27:23,300
I mean, they're children living in the middle of all of this.

602
00:27:23,300 --> 00:27:25,300
Would you have wanted me to say no

603
00:27:25,300 --> 00:27:27,300
when the company insisted I come in?

604
00:27:27,300 --> 00:27:28,300
Doc, she's going to hit you.

605
00:27:28,300 --> 00:27:29,300
No, it's not.

606
00:27:29,300 --> 00:27:30,300
No, I'm just tired.

607
00:27:30,300 --> 00:27:31,300
I'm sorry.

608
00:27:31,300 --> 00:27:33,300
Well, let's go out and find Buddy Kim.

609
00:27:33,300 --> 00:27:35,300
Okay. I could use some air.

610
00:27:38,300 --> 00:27:40,300
Let's see. What else can I hate?

611
00:27:40,300 --> 00:27:44,300
I wish the children hadn't wandered off.

612
00:27:44,300 --> 00:27:46,300
You think it's dangerous down there in the rocks?

613
00:27:46,300 --> 00:27:49,300
No. Besides, you know how the boys love the beach.

614
00:27:49,300 --> 00:27:51,300
The ocean, the rocks,

615
00:27:51,300 --> 00:27:54,300
everything makes me feel so unimportant to myself.

616
00:27:54,300 --> 00:27:55,300
Well, you'll like it here.

617
00:27:55,300 --> 00:27:56,300
Where do you meet the others?

618
00:27:56,300 --> 00:27:58,300
Then you'll feel really unimportant.

619
00:27:58,300 --> 00:28:00,300
I guess we better get back to straighten things out.

620
00:28:00,300 --> 00:28:03,300
The sand is probably destroying everything in there.

621
00:28:03,300 --> 00:28:04,300
Mr. Brewster?

622
00:28:04,300 --> 00:28:05,300
Hi.

623
00:28:05,300 --> 00:28:07,300
I'm your new roommate.

624
00:28:07,300 --> 00:28:09,300
I'm Mr. James, Security Officer for the command.

625
00:28:09,300 --> 00:28:11,300
I just heard from the gate you'd arrived.

626
00:28:11,300 --> 00:28:12,300
This is my wife.

627
00:28:12,300 --> 00:28:13,300
How do you do?

628
00:28:13,300 --> 00:28:15,300
I hope you'll be comfortable here, Mr. Brewster.

629
00:28:15,300 --> 00:28:16,300
Thank you.

630
00:28:16,300 --> 00:28:17,300
I'm glad I caught you.

631
00:28:17,300 --> 00:28:18,300
I hope it won't be inconvenient,

632
00:28:18,300 --> 00:28:19,300
but you're the last member to arrive

633
00:28:19,300 --> 00:28:20,300
and the Colonel's giving a welcome briefing

634
00:28:20,300 --> 00:28:22,300
I think you'd like to attend.

635
00:28:22,300 --> 00:28:23,300
If you don't mind, Mr. Brewster?

636
00:28:23,300 --> 00:28:25,300
No, of course not.

637
00:28:25,300 --> 00:28:26,300
You'll come back as soon as you can.

638
00:28:26,300 --> 00:28:27,300
Sure, I will.

639
00:28:27,300 --> 00:28:29,300
And if me and the kids aren't there when you get back,

640
00:28:29,300 --> 00:28:31,300
just accept them.

641
00:28:36,300 --> 00:28:40,300
Well, time to throw myself on the bed and heave in sobs.

642
00:28:40,300 --> 00:28:42,300
Hello.

643
00:28:42,300 --> 00:28:44,300
I'm Freida Johnson.

644
00:28:44,300 --> 00:28:45,300
I live in the next trailer.

645
00:28:45,300 --> 00:28:46,300
I'm Ann Brewster.

646
00:28:46,300 --> 00:28:47,300
How do you do?

647
00:28:47,300 --> 00:28:48,300
I'm your Ethel Mertz.

648
00:28:48,300 --> 00:28:49,300
You just arrived.

649
00:28:49,300 --> 00:28:52,300
Everything certainly is strange and different here.

650
00:28:52,300 --> 00:28:54,300
I know just how you feel.

651
00:28:54,300 --> 00:28:56,300
I thought I'd die the first few weeks away

652
00:28:56,300 --> 00:28:57,300
from my folks and friends.

653
00:28:57,300 --> 00:29:01,300
It's the feeling of living so close to the end of the world, maybe.

654
00:29:01,300 --> 00:29:02,300
After what?

655
00:29:02,300 --> 00:29:03,300
You don't think of it like that.

656
00:29:03,300 --> 00:29:05,300
Do you have any children?

657
00:29:05,300 --> 00:29:06,300
Two boys.

658
00:29:06,300 --> 00:29:07,300
They're on the beach somewhere.

659
00:29:07,300 --> 00:29:08,300
How old are they?

660
00:29:08,300 --> 00:29:10,300
Twelve and ten.

661
00:29:10,300 --> 00:29:11,300
Oh, that'll be great for Edie.

662
00:29:11,300 --> 00:29:12,300
She's eleven.

663
00:29:12,300 --> 00:29:15,300
Well, I better get my laundry on the line.

664
00:29:15,300 --> 00:29:18,300
Oh, by the way, we're having a weenie roast out here tonight.

665
00:29:18,300 --> 00:29:19,300
Why don't you come?

666
00:29:19,300 --> 00:29:20,300
It's really for the kids.

667
00:29:20,300 --> 00:29:22,300
Oh, that'd be very nice.

668
00:29:22,300 --> 00:29:23,300
Thank you so much.

669
00:29:23,300 --> 00:29:24,300
Good, then we'll see you later.

670
00:29:24,300 --> 00:29:29,300
And slowly lock the doors and hide in the closet.

671
00:29:29,300 --> 00:29:35,300
[Music]

672
00:29:35,300 --> 00:29:37,300
We're almost home.

673
00:29:37,300 --> 00:29:38,300
We've hit Yosemite.

674
00:29:38,300 --> 00:29:42,300
[Panting]

675
00:29:42,300 --> 00:29:43,300
Here, catch!

676
00:29:43,300 --> 00:29:44,300
Just a minute!

677
00:29:44,300 --> 00:29:46,300
Come on, run!

678
00:29:46,300 --> 00:29:50,300
Let me get over by a sharper rock.

679
00:29:50,300 --> 00:29:52,300
Nice throw.

680
00:29:52,300 --> 00:29:54,300
You only had an hour to line it up.

681
00:29:54,300 --> 00:29:57,300
Hey, bud, come here!

682
00:29:57,300 --> 00:29:58,300
Ow!

683
00:29:58,300 --> 00:29:59,300
Ow!

684
00:29:59,300 --> 00:30:00,300
Ow!

685
00:30:00,300 --> 00:30:03,300
Gee, bud, I bet it's a real cave.

686
00:30:03,300 --> 00:30:04,300
Yeah.

687
00:30:04,300 --> 00:30:07,300
This is a perfect place to make our delicious Roquefort cheese.

688
00:30:07,300 --> 00:30:08,300
Yeah.

689
00:30:08,300 --> 00:30:13,300
Grendel, you home?

690
00:30:13,300 --> 00:30:19,300
It's a naturally occurring comedy club.

691
00:30:19,300 --> 00:30:27,300
Gee, do you think we discovered this cave?

692
00:30:27,300 --> 00:30:28,300
Maybe.

693
00:30:28,300 --> 00:30:30,300
What a day.

694
00:30:30,300 --> 00:30:32,300
First that thing in the sky and now this place.

695
00:30:32,300 --> 00:30:34,300
Then we played with a ball? Wow.

696
00:30:34,300 --> 00:30:36,300
Are you scared of what you saw?

697
00:30:36,300 --> 00:30:37,300
You?

698
00:30:37,300 --> 00:30:39,300
No.

699
00:30:39,300 --> 00:30:40,300
Do you think it'll come back?

700
00:30:40,300 --> 00:30:41,300
I hope so.

701
00:30:41,300 --> 00:30:43,300
So do I.

702
00:30:43,300 --> 00:30:44,300
You bet.

703
00:30:44,300 --> 00:30:46,300
Then we can show it to Dad and prove we weren't making things up.

704
00:30:46,300 --> 00:30:48,300
What happened?

705
00:30:48,300 --> 00:30:51,300
Kind of spookier.

706
00:30:51,300 --> 00:30:52,300
Yeah.

707
00:30:53,300 --> 00:30:57,300
It's all dark back there. Maybe at least another cave.

708
00:30:57,300 --> 00:31:00,300
You better stay here again.

709
00:31:00,300 --> 00:31:07,300
Wow. Look at that giant cave squid stinging him to death, sucking the blood right out of him. Cool.

710
00:31:07,300 --> 00:31:11,300
Hi.

711
00:31:11,300 --> 00:31:12,300
You scared me.

712
00:31:12,300 --> 00:31:14,300
Hi.

713
00:31:14,300 --> 00:31:16,300
We're the children of the damned you've heard about.

714
00:31:16,300 --> 00:31:17,300
We found our cave.

715
00:31:17,300 --> 00:31:18,300
We didn't know anyone knew about it.

716
00:31:18,300 --> 00:31:20,300
We have secret club meetings here.

717
00:31:20,300 --> 00:31:22,300
My name's Edie Johnson.

718
00:31:22,300 --> 00:31:24,300
I saw you move in next door to us.

719
00:31:24,300 --> 00:31:25,300
This guy.

720
00:31:25,300 --> 00:31:26,300
Who are you?

721
00:31:26,300 --> 00:31:28,300
I'm Bud Brewster. This is my kid brother Ken.

722
00:31:28,300 --> 00:31:29,300
Hi.

723
00:31:29,300 --> 00:31:32,300
This is Buster, Tim, George and Helen.

724
00:31:32,300 --> 00:31:34,300
I'm too old for this group really.

725
00:31:34,300 --> 00:31:35,300
Your father wanted to work here?

726
00:31:35,300 --> 00:31:37,300
Yeah, he's what you call a technician.

727
00:31:37,300 --> 00:31:42,300
He knows everything about orbits and satellites and hydrogen and missiles and warheads.

728
00:31:42,300 --> 00:31:43,300
So does mine.

729
00:31:43,300 --> 00:31:45,300
Have you seen it yet, the Thunder?

730
00:31:45,300 --> 00:31:47,300
It's the biggest one in the world.

731
00:31:47,300 --> 00:31:48,300
It's a six-stage rocket.

732
00:31:48,300 --> 00:31:53,300
It takes a satellite with a hydrogen warhead and the satellite will be hundreds of miles up in a year.

733
00:31:53,300 --> 00:32:02,580
It's a

734
00:32:02,580 --> 00:32:04,300
Remind me to never be a child.

735
00:32:04,300 --> 00:32:10,300
Lord of the Flies action figures.

736
00:32:10,300 --> 00:32:16,300
Is your mom sitting back in your trailer depressed and warning the life she can never have?

737
00:32:16,300 --> 00:32:17,300
Mine too.

738
00:32:19,300 --> 00:32:22,300
Say, have any of you said the darndest thing lately?

739
00:32:22,300 --> 00:32:30,300
Two billion dollars and we made a poll.

740
00:32:30,300 --> 00:32:34,300
There it is.

741
00:32:34,300 --> 00:32:35,300
Wow.

742
00:32:35,300 --> 00:32:36,300
Isn't it terrific?

743
00:32:36,300 --> 00:32:37,300
Yeah, it sure is.

744
00:32:37,300 --> 00:32:41,300
The Edward Teller Home Security System.

745
00:32:41,300 --> 00:32:42,300
Magnificent.

746
00:32:42,300 --> 00:32:43,300
All right, beat it kids.

747
00:32:43,300 --> 00:32:44,300
You know you don't belong here.

748
00:32:44,300 --> 00:32:45,300
Okay, okay.

749
00:32:45,300 --> 00:32:46,300
I was only showing them the Thunder.

750
00:32:46,300 --> 00:32:47,300
Come on, let's move.

751
00:32:47,300 --> 00:32:48,300
All right.

752
00:32:48,300 --> 00:32:49,300
I'm with you.

753
00:32:49,300 --> 00:32:50,300
But don't you moon me.

754
00:32:50,300 --> 00:32:51,300
Wow.

755
00:32:51,300 --> 00:32:52,300
Toss me that warhead.

756
00:32:52,300 --> 00:32:53,300
Here, throw it to me.

757
00:32:53,300 --> 00:32:54,300
Catch it.

758
00:32:54,300 --> 00:32:55,300
Does anyone else think this isn't much fun?

759
00:32:55,300 --> 00:32:56,300
Hey, look up there.

760
00:32:56,300 --> 00:32:57,300
What is it, son?

761
00:32:57,300 --> 00:32:58,300
It's a

762
00:32:58,300 --> 00:33:13,300
It's cleaning that cave like a white tornado.

763
00:33:13,300 --> 00:33:21,300
I saw nothing like this in Antwerp.

764
00:33:21,300 --> 00:33:23,300
Come on.

765
00:33:23,300 --> 00:33:25,300
Let's watch them come-on-ing.

766
00:33:25,300 --> 00:33:28,300
Hey, hey, we're the children.

767
00:33:28,300 --> 00:33:30,300
People say we children around.

768
00:33:30,300 --> 00:33:32,300
We're too busy children-ing.

769
00:33:32,300 --> 00:33:33,300
Okay, yeah.

770
00:33:33,300 --> 00:33:34,300
That's enough.

771
00:33:34,300 --> 00:33:35,300
Thank you.

772
00:33:35,300 --> 00:33:36,300
Children.

773
00:33:36,300 --> 00:33:44,300
Yes, I will take money from my dad's wallet and send it to soupy sales.

774
00:33:44,300 --> 00:33:48,300
Matt, you can call me Ray.

775
00:33:48,300 --> 00:33:49,300
No.

776
00:33:49,300 --> 00:33:50,300
You're on warning.

777
00:33:53,300 --> 00:33:56,300
Wow, the space people are passing a gallstone.

778
00:33:56,300 --> 00:34:02,300
With pinpoint accuracy.

779
00:34:02,300 --> 00:34:04,300
Hang on, Neil's bore is using the toaster.

780
00:34:04,300 --> 00:34:06,300
Let's just wait a minute, gentlemen.

781
00:34:06,300 --> 00:34:07,300
Lights will be on in a minute, probably a fuse.

782
00:34:07,300 --> 00:34:08,300
Check 'em, please.

783
00:34:08,300 --> 00:34:10,300
General, at this point in time, I am scared.

784
00:34:10,300 --> 00:34:12,300
Yep, scared, sir.

785
00:34:12,300 --> 00:34:17,300
If I could just graze that 9-pin, get the spare.

786
00:34:20,300 --> 00:34:23,300
Bud's got the Steve McGarrett hair going.

787
00:34:23,300 --> 00:34:28,300
We disproved God while you were gone.

788
00:34:28,300 --> 00:34:31,300
There.

789
00:34:31,300 --> 00:34:32,300
That's better.

790
00:34:32,300 --> 00:34:34,300
Now what was I mesmerizing you with?

791
00:34:34,300 --> 00:34:36,300
Sorry for the interruption, gentlemen.

792
00:34:36,300 --> 00:34:39,300
It's nice to know we're no longer in the dark.

793
00:34:39,300 --> 00:34:40,300
Sir!

794
00:34:40,300 --> 00:34:41,300
Ha ha ha ha ha!

795
00:34:41,300 --> 00:34:42,300
Sir!

796
00:34:42,300 --> 00:34:44,300
Getting back to the launching of the Thunderer.

797
00:34:44,300 --> 00:34:47,300
Mermaids are really hitting today.

798
00:34:49,300 --> 00:34:50,300
Hi, Mayor.

799
00:34:50,300 --> 00:34:53,300
This will complete the Thunderer.

800
00:34:53,300 --> 00:34:59,300
Sessions presents Bald Gold.

801
00:34:59,300 --> 00:35:04,300
Man, the moon doggy's really gone to sea, man.

802
00:35:04,300 --> 00:35:09,300
I'm washing my socks.

803
00:35:09,300 --> 00:35:15,300
How's the fishing, Colonel?

804
00:35:15,300 --> 00:35:17,300
Dr. Warman.

805
00:35:17,300 --> 00:35:18,300
Any luck?

806
00:35:18,300 --> 00:35:19,300
Ha ha.

807
00:35:19,300 --> 00:35:20,300
Not a bite.

808
00:35:20,300 --> 00:35:22,300
Do sailfish hit on bologna?

809
00:35:22,300 --> 00:35:26,300
Wonderful day.

810
00:35:26,300 --> 00:35:28,300
The sky looks so innocent.

811
00:35:28,300 --> 00:35:29,300
What?

812
00:35:29,300 --> 00:35:31,300
Doctor, will we succeed tomorrow?

813
00:35:31,300 --> 00:35:33,300
I see no reason why not.

814
00:35:33,300 --> 00:35:35,300
How time flies.

815
00:35:35,300 --> 00:35:38,300
Seems like yesterday the first satellite orbited through space.

816
00:35:38,300 --> 00:35:39,300
Yes.

817
00:35:39,300 --> 00:35:41,300
Now we launch my godchild.

818
00:35:41,300 --> 00:35:42,300
She's five.

819
00:35:42,300 --> 00:35:44,300
I suppose people will get used to the Thunderer.

820
00:35:44,300 --> 00:35:45,300
Its implications.

821
00:35:45,300 --> 00:35:46,300
Hey, Dad.

822
00:35:46,300 --> 00:35:48,300
Hello, son.

823
00:35:48,300 --> 00:35:50,300
Hi, Dad.

824
00:35:50,300 --> 00:35:51,300
Hi, Phyllis.

825
00:35:51,300 --> 00:35:53,300
How's fishing, Dad?

826
00:35:53,300 --> 00:35:54,300
Not very good.

827
00:35:54,300 --> 00:35:55,300
Catch anything?

828
00:35:55,300 --> 00:35:56,300
Probably the sniffles.

829
00:35:56,300 --> 00:35:58,300
Water cold?

830
00:35:58,300 --> 00:35:59,300
A little.

831
00:35:59,300 --> 00:36:00,300
Come on, Phyllis, let's get dressed.

832
00:36:00,300 --> 00:36:01,300
See you, kids.

833
00:36:01,300 --> 00:36:04,300
Remember when sex wasn't a job?

834
00:36:04,300 --> 00:36:06,300
Life's a wonderful thing, Doctor.

835
00:36:06,300 --> 00:36:08,300
Let's hope we can preserve it for them.

836
00:36:08,300 --> 00:36:11,300
So, you're a commie rat, huh?

837
00:36:13,300 --> 00:36:14,300
What's going on?

838
00:36:14,300 --> 00:36:19,300
Intestine stuffed with nitrates and pig snouts.

839
00:36:19,300 --> 00:36:21,300
Hey, look, here.

840
00:36:21,300 --> 00:36:23,300
Hey, watch it, kids, huh?

841
00:36:23,300 --> 00:36:25,300
Come and get them while they're hot boys.

842
00:36:25,300 --> 00:36:26,300
Plenty more with these game drums.

843
00:36:26,300 --> 00:36:27,300
Oh, honey, just put them on the table.

844
00:36:27,300 --> 00:36:28,300
We're up to here with hot dogs.

845
00:36:28,300 --> 00:36:30,300
God, it's Uncle Fester in shorts.

846
00:36:30,300 --> 00:36:31,300
Yeah, I know.

847
00:36:31,300 --> 00:36:33,300
Well, if this parent teacher's meeting...

848
00:36:33,300 --> 00:36:34,300
Ah!

849
00:36:34,300 --> 00:36:36,300
...on the spot, they kept saying,

850
00:36:36,300 --> 00:36:37,300
"When is it going to end?"

851
00:36:37,300 --> 00:36:39,300
Year after year of racing, racing,

852
00:36:39,300 --> 00:36:41,300
trying to find something bigger and better

853
00:36:41,300 --> 00:36:43,300
to blow ourselves off the planet.

854
00:36:43,300 --> 00:36:45,300
When they ask me these questions,

855
00:36:45,300 --> 00:36:46,300
what do I tell them?

856
00:36:46,300 --> 00:36:49,300
You just say to them that down there stands the Thunderer.

857
00:36:49,300 --> 00:36:51,300
And what are we waiting for?

858
00:36:51,300 --> 00:36:54,300
Hank, dear, let's not be serious tonight, huh?

859
00:36:54,300 --> 00:36:55,300
Let's get to the wife swapping.

860
00:36:55,300 --> 00:36:57,300
It's your first day here, Dave.

861
00:36:57,300 --> 00:36:58,300
What's your viewpoint?

862
00:36:58,300 --> 00:37:00,300
Same as my wife's.

863
00:37:00,300 --> 00:37:03,300
In all its history, our country's never started a war.

864
00:37:03,300 --> 00:37:04,300
The Thunderer is to prevent war.

865
00:37:04,300 --> 00:37:07,300
I still say that when that satellite gets up there

866
00:37:07,300 --> 00:37:09,300
with the Thunderer and it gets into its orbit, we should...

867
00:37:09,300 --> 00:37:10,300
We should take a vacation.

868
00:37:10,300 --> 00:37:11,300
That's what you need, Hank.

869
00:37:11,300 --> 00:37:12,300
A nice vacation.

870
00:37:12,300 --> 00:37:14,300
Hank could kill everybody if you let him.

871
00:37:14,300 --> 00:37:17,300
Dave, why don't you and Hank take a swim, huh?

872
00:37:17,300 --> 00:37:18,300
Come on, Johnson, let's take a dip with the kids.

873
00:37:18,300 --> 00:37:19,300
What do you say?

874
00:37:19,300 --> 00:37:20,300
That's a good idea.

875
00:37:20,300 --> 00:37:21,300
Edie?

876
00:37:21,300 --> 00:37:22,300
Yes, Daddy?

877
00:37:22,300 --> 00:37:24,300
Want to go for a swim with me, honey?

878
00:37:24,300 --> 00:37:25,300
Sure, Daddy, I'll go.

879
00:37:25,300 --> 00:37:28,300
Oh, no, his shorts.

880
00:37:28,300 --> 00:37:31,300
That's right, his horrible shorts.

881
00:37:31,300 --> 00:37:35,300
I'd go, but I'm high.

882
00:37:38,300 --> 00:37:41,300
I think I had too many hot dogs, Daddy.

883
00:37:41,300 --> 00:37:43,300
I'd better not go for a swim.

884
00:37:43,300 --> 00:37:45,300
How about the rest of you kids?

885
00:37:45,300 --> 00:37:46,300
Anybody want to go for a dip?

886
00:37:46,300 --> 00:37:47,300
Bud, Ken?

887
00:37:47,300 --> 00:37:49,300
Francois, Abdul, Vyeshdoshlav.

888
00:37:49,300 --> 00:37:50,300
Thanks, Dad.

889
00:37:50,300 --> 00:37:51,300
Edie, I'll race you to the cliff.

890
00:37:51,300 --> 00:37:52,300
Sure.

891
00:37:52,300 --> 00:37:55,300
Our daughter sure got over her stomach.

892
00:37:55,300 --> 00:37:56,300
Ain't gonna hurry, didn't she?

893
00:37:56,300 --> 00:37:57,300
She sure did.

894
00:37:57,300 --> 00:37:58,300
You ready for the big plunge?

895
00:37:58,300 --> 00:37:59,300
Yeah, sure.

896
00:37:59,300 --> 00:38:00,300
Hello, Joe.

897
00:38:00,300 --> 00:38:01,300
Hi.

898
00:38:01,300 --> 00:38:02,300
Hi.

899
00:38:02,300 --> 00:38:03,300
Hi.

900
00:38:03,300 --> 00:38:04,300
This is Peg and Joe Gamble and Brewster.

901
00:38:04,300 --> 00:38:05,300
Hi.

902
00:38:05,300 --> 00:38:06,300
Nice to know you.

903
00:38:06,300 --> 00:38:08,300
Hi.

904
00:38:08,300 --> 00:38:11,300
Well, we're a little late, but then, of course, nobody invited us.

905
00:38:11,300 --> 00:38:12,300
Joe, we were invited.

906
00:38:12,300 --> 00:38:14,300
You fell asleep, don't you remember?

907
00:38:14,300 --> 00:38:16,300
Joe, stop carrying that chip on your shoulder.

908
00:38:16,300 --> 00:38:18,300
Well, he isn't feeling very well tonight, Freda.

909
00:38:18,300 --> 00:38:20,300
My wife is just trying to be polite.

910
00:38:20,300 --> 00:38:22,300
She means I'm tight.

911
00:38:22,300 --> 00:38:24,300
Did you get that job, Joe?

912
00:38:24,300 --> 00:38:25,300
No, I flunked a test.

913
00:38:25,300 --> 00:38:26,300
Puked on the blue book.

914
00:38:26,300 --> 00:38:28,300
Peg will have to go on bringing in the bankroll.

915
00:38:28,300 --> 00:38:29,300
Please, Joe.

916
00:38:29,300 --> 00:38:31,300
I'm done with roller derby.

917
00:38:31,300 --> 00:38:32,300
Where's Jim?

918
00:38:32,300 --> 00:38:34,300
Oh, he's with the other children.

919
00:38:34,300 --> 00:38:37,300
He's always running off without telling us where he's going.

920
00:38:37,300 --> 00:38:38,300
Wow.

921
00:38:38,300 --> 00:38:39,300
If I were that kid's real father, I'd...

922
00:38:39,300 --> 00:38:41,300
But you're not his father, and I'm not your wife,

923
00:38:41,300 --> 00:38:45,300
so I can afford to tell you a few things that have been on my mind, Joe Gamble.

924
00:38:45,300 --> 00:38:46,300
He's a spoiled brat.

925
00:38:46,300 --> 00:38:47,300
He won't drink with me.

926
00:38:47,300 --> 00:38:48,300
Him?

927
00:38:48,300 --> 00:38:49,300
Where is he?

928
00:38:49,300 --> 00:38:50,300
Him?

929
00:38:50,300 --> 00:38:51,300
(Barks)

930
00:38:51,300 --> 00:38:52,300
Him?

931
00:38:52,300 --> 00:38:53,300
(Barks)

932
00:38:53,300 --> 00:38:59,300
(Music)

933
00:38:59,300 --> 00:39:05,300
Four, three, two, one, blast off!

934
00:39:05,300 --> 00:39:06,300
Yay!

935
00:39:06,300 --> 00:39:07,300
Oh, for God...

936
00:39:07,300 --> 00:39:08,300
What?

937
00:39:08,300 --> 00:39:09,300
Oh, for...

938
00:39:09,300 --> 00:39:10,300
Oh, man.

939
00:39:10,300 --> 00:39:12,300
Oh, okay, got to be careful around that.

940
00:39:12,300 --> 00:39:14,300
Remember, don't turn it on until I say, okay?

941
00:39:14,300 --> 00:39:15,300
What?

942
00:39:15,300 --> 00:39:16,300
Turn it on?

943
00:39:16,300 --> 00:39:41,300
No, I'll... I'll... I'll... I'll... I'll... I'll... I'll... I'll... I'll... I'll... I'll... I'll...

944
00:39:41,300 --> 00:39:44,300
Model Rocketry, I'll show you Model Rocketry.

945
00:39:44,300 --> 00:39:46,300
Hey, look at what I got.

946
00:39:46,300 --> 00:39:50,300
(Thunder)

947
00:39:50,300 --> 00:39:55,300
In fact, now that I think about it, does the word "model" make any sense at all?

948
00:39:55,300 --> 00:39:56,300
No!

949
00:39:56,300 --> 00:40:00,300
What I got going is way beyond model rockets.

950
00:40:00,300 --> 00:40:01,300
I got a rocket!

951
00:40:01,300 --> 00:40:02,300
Go get the monkey.

952
00:40:02,300 --> 00:40:03,300
Yes.

953
00:40:03,300 --> 00:40:07,300
Sure, at this point, I'm lagging behind the other superpowers in the race to dominate space,

954
00:40:07,300 --> 00:40:12,300
but as soon as I launch my first monkey into space, there is going to be such...

955
00:40:12,300 --> 00:40:14,300
I was scared to go into space.

956
00:40:14,300 --> 00:40:15,300
Oh, weird training.

957
00:40:15,300 --> 00:40:17,300
Now, shut up and get in the centrifuge.

958
00:40:17,300 --> 00:40:18,300
Okay.

959
00:40:18,300 --> 00:40:21,300
See, the way I figure it, I got a monkey.

960
00:40:21,300 --> 00:40:25,300
Why not develop a space program around that monkey?

961
00:40:25,300 --> 00:40:27,300
No reason at all.

962
00:40:27,300 --> 00:40:28,300
Monkey in centrifuge, ma'am.

963
00:40:28,300 --> 00:40:30,300
Of course, I can't take all the credit.

964
00:40:30,300 --> 00:40:34,300
It was Brain Guy here who pointed out to me that we have a monkey.

965
00:40:34,300 --> 00:40:35,300
Now, now, don't be modest.

966
00:40:35,300 --> 00:40:38,300
You're the one who realized we have a monkey.

967
00:40:38,300 --> 00:40:39,300
I suppose I did.

968
00:40:39,300 --> 00:40:40,300
(Chuckles)

969
00:40:40,300 --> 00:40:42,300
There's a sharp thing in my side.

970
00:40:42,300 --> 00:40:43,300
How?

971
00:40:43,300 --> 00:40:49,300
Oh, it's simply the pin that holds the passenger compartment to the centrifuge itself.

972
00:40:49,300 --> 00:40:52,300
I don't suppose I...

973
00:40:52,300 --> 00:41:02,300
(Screaming)

974
00:41:02,300 --> 00:41:06,300
That was fun.

975
00:41:06,300 --> 00:41:07,300
Let's do it again.

976
00:41:07,300 --> 00:41:14,300
The point is, Nelson, you can just sit down because I got a space program.

977
00:41:14,300 --> 00:41:16,300
(Laughing)

978
00:41:16,300 --> 00:41:18,300
Come on now, big fella.

979
00:41:18,300 --> 00:41:20,300
Let's take another ride.

980
00:41:20,300 --> 00:41:24,300
(Singing)

981
00:41:24,300 --> 00:41:26,300
Oh, don't turn it on.

982
00:41:26,300 --> 00:41:27,300
(Laughing)

983
00:41:27,300 --> 00:41:29,300
For Moby's sign, live and learn.

984
00:41:29,300 --> 00:41:41,300
(Laughing)

985
00:41:41,300 --> 00:41:43,300
You might want to put out your shirt sleeve.

986
00:41:43,300 --> 00:41:44,300
Yeah, oh, thanks.

987
00:41:44,300 --> 00:41:45,300
We just blew you up.

988
00:41:45,300 --> 00:41:50,300
Good deal.

989
00:41:50,300 --> 00:41:55,300
Oh, they're trying to get as far away from Jackie Coogan in tiny shorts as possible.

990
00:41:55,300 --> 00:42:02,300
Well, the pilot for Baywatch was very different from the series, wasn't it?

991
00:42:02,300 --> 00:42:08,300
Has he ever eaten or been out in the sun at all?

992
00:42:08,300 --> 00:42:18,300
Yep, we lose a kid a week doing this, but it's still fun.

993
00:42:18,300 --> 00:42:21,300
A little help?

994
00:42:21,300 --> 00:42:30,300
Yes, we're almost to Switzerland, then we'll be safe.

995
00:42:30,300 --> 00:42:33,300
Oh, yes, Edie can wear her swimsuit another three or four years.

996
00:42:33,300 --> 00:42:34,300
It's fine.

997
00:42:34,300 --> 00:42:36,300
Poor kid.

998
00:42:36,300 --> 00:42:42,300
We will name this new colony Budtown.

999
00:42:42,300 --> 00:42:49,300
Well, they ran all the way to the Antarctic.

1000
00:42:49,300 --> 00:42:51,300
Where do we go?

1001
00:42:51,300 --> 00:42:52,300
Up this way.

1002
00:42:52,300 --> 00:42:59,300
Are you visiting Fred Flintstone at work?

1003
00:42:59,300 --> 00:43:03,300
Hey, a glowing challah.

1004
00:43:03,300 --> 00:43:17,300
Hey, guys, we got a new third base.

1005
00:43:17,300 --> 00:43:23,300
Two weenies, one with mustard.

1006
00:43:23,300 --> 00:43:25,300
You knew what would be here.

1007
00:43:25,300 --> 00:43:27,300
Did it tell you?

1008
00:43:27,300 --> 00:43:28,300
Yes.

1009
00:43:28,300 --> 00:43:31,300
It said, "I will be here."

1010
00:43:31,300 --> 00:43:33,300
Is he wearing a miniskirt?

1011
00:43:33,300 --> 00:43:34,300
I don't know.

1012
00:43:34,300 --> 00:43:35,300
You're going to be the leader.

1013
00:43:35,300 --> 00:43:38,300
You'll have to do what I tell you to.

1014
00:43:38,300 --> 00:43:40,300
I'm getting out of here.

1015
00:43:40,300 --> 00:43:44,300
I have an appointment with my broker.

1016
00:43:44,300 --> 00:43:49,300
He's strong for a man his age.

1017
00:43:49,300 --> 00:43:51,300
I can't move.

1018
00:43:51,300 --> 00:43:58,300
I think it's because of my allergies.

1019
00:43:58,300 --> 00:43:59,300
You can now.

1020
00:43:59,300 --> 00:44:02,300
Well, now I just don't want to.

1021
00:44:02,300 --> 00:44:03,300
Try.

1022
00:44:03,300 --> 00:44:06,300
Your thought commandeth you.

1023
00:44:06,300 --> 00:44:09,300
From now on, when I ask you to do something, we'll do it together.

1024
00:44:09,300 --> 00:44:10,300
Wow.

1025
00:44:10,300 --> 00:44:11,300
Yes, Bud.

1026
00:44:11,300 --> 00:44:12,300
Yes, Bud.

1027
00:44:12,300 --> 00:44:13,300
Sure.

1028
00:44:13,300 --> 00:44:20,300
Sorry about the rock and all.

1029
00:44:20,300 --> 00:44:24,300
So I assume you kids are the all-powerful rulers of Earth?

1030
00:44:24,300 --> 00:44:26,300
Hey, kids, enjoy my silly putty qualities.

1031
00:44:26,300 --> 00:44:32,300
I can lift images off the funny papers for you.

1032
00:44:32,300 --> 00:44:33,300
We're married with children.

1033
00:44:33,300 --> 00:44:35,300
It's blaring away in there.

1034
00:44:35,300 --> 00:44:36,300
Hank, is Edie back yet?

1035
00:44:36,300 --> 00:44:37,300
Just a minute.

1036
00:44:37,300 --> 00:44:39,300
Good, yeah.

1037
00:44:39,300 --> 00:44:40,300
Yeah.

1038
00:44:40,300 --> 00:44:41,300
Oh, it's all right.

1039
00:44:41,300 --> 00:44:42,300
Thank you very much.

1040
00:44:42,300 --> 00:44:43,300
Where have you been?

1041
00:44:43,300 --> 00:44:44,300
Sorry, Mother.

1042
00:44:44,300 --> 00:44:46,300
I oughta wallop to both of you.

1043
00:44:46,300 --> 00:44:49,300
Wearing your mother like that, stay on till almost nine.

1044
00:44:49,300 --> 00:44:51,300
We were just on the beach.

1045
00:44:51,300 --> 00:44:52,300
You knew this was our first day here.

1046
00:44:52,300 --> 00:44:55,300
You made me walk up and down the beach hunting for you and your brother.

1047
00:44:55,300 --> 00:44:56,300
Dave, stop pounding at me.

1048
00:44:56,300 --> 00:44:57,300
Go get undressed.

1049
00:44:57,300 --> 00:44:58,300
Tell him, Bud.

1050
00:44:58,300 --> 00:44:59,300
Tell him.

1051
00:44:59,300 --> 00:45:00,300
Tell us what?

1052
00:45:00,300 --> 00:45:02,300
Bud's omnipotent.

1053
00:45:02,300 --> 00:45:04,300
We can tell him, can't we, Bud?

1054
00:45:04,300 --> 00:45:05,300
Blow and blob.

1055
00:45:05,300 --> 00:45:11,300
We need a decision on this one.

1056
00:45:11,300 --> 00:45:14,300
Yes, I know.

1057
00:45:14,300 --> 00:45:15,300
What's the matter?

1058
00:45:15,300 --> 00:45:17,300
What are you talking to yourself for?

1059
00:45:17,300 --> 00:45:18,300
You sick?

1060
00:45:18,300 --> 00:45:19,300
No, I'm all right.

1061
00:45:19,300 --> 00:45:22,300
I've just had nothing but hot dogs for eight days.

1062
00:45:22,300 --> 00:45:24,300
Weren't you gonna tell him, Bud?

1063
00:45:24,300 --> 00:45:27,300
I'm sick of wearing tough skins, Mom.

1064
00:45:27,300 --> 00:45:31,300
We found something that fell out of the sky this afternoon.

1065
00:45:31,300 --> 00:45:32,300
We know where it is.

1066
00:45:32,300 --> 00:45:33,300
The sky?

1067
00:45:33,300 --> 00:45:35,300
Bud's telling the truth.

1068
00:45:35,300 --> 00:45:37,300
I saw it too.

1069
00:45:37,300 --> 00:45:39,300
It fell out of the sky.

1070
00:45:39,300 --> 00:45:42,300
Well, you've gotta believe him.

1071
00:45:42,300 --> 00:45:44,300
How long did it take you to dream up that yarn?

1072
00:45:44,300 --> 00:45:45,300
I didn't dream it up.

1073
00:45:45,300 --> 00:45:47,300
You think a lot like that's gonna make it all right, huh?

1074
00:45:47,300 --> 00:45:48,300
For staying out until all hours?

1075
00:45:48,300 --> 00:45:50,300
It's not a lie.

1076
00:45:50,300 --> 00:45:51,300
Something's wrong.

1077
00:45:51,300 --> 00:45:52,300
I know it is.

1078
00:45:52,300 --> 00:45:53,300
Something is wrong.

1079
00:45:53,300 --> 00:45:54,300
Look, you're upsetting him by now.

1080
00:45:54,300 --> 00:45:55,300
Let's go to bed.

1081
00:45:55,300 --> 00:45:56,300
Come on.

1082
00:45:56,300 --> 00:45:57,300
Dad, you've gotta believe.

1083
00:45:57,300 --> 00:45:58,300
Believe what?

1084
00:45:58,300 --> 00:45:59,300
Some crazy story you made up for an excuse?

1085
00:45:59,300 --> 00:46:00,300
Listen, for two cents I...

1086
00:46:00,300 --> 00:46:03,300
Thou hast angered Bud.

1087
00:46:03,300 --> 00:46:04,300
Come on.

1088
00:46:04,300 --> 00:46:05,300
Come on, boy, come on.

1089
00:46:05,300 --> 00:46:08,300
Pork chop going through aorta.

1090
00:46:08,300 --> 00:46:11,300
